128: ## Reactivation rule
129: 
130: Another deleted component may return only when a named current workload demonstrates all of the following:
131: 
132: 1. absence causes a reproduced failure, duplicated Effect, false completion, unrecoverable uncertainty, authority confusion or material manual recovery cost;
133: 2. Host, Runtime, the provider, operating system or domain authority cannot own the responsibility more cleanly;
134: 3. at least two real consumers need the same retained semantics before a shared abstraction is introduced;
135: 4. total implementation and operating cost is lower than direct adapters;
136: 5. every retained field and service has a deletion condition.
